You don't send the time. The time is relative. The server getting the initial request should start the ticks. Your scenario is completely hackable.

If I understood your problem you can use something like this Promise.timeout:
Promise.timeout = function(timeout, promise){
  return Promise.race([
  promise,
  new Promise(function(resolve, reject){
    setTimeout(function() { reject('Timed out'); }, timeout);
  })
]);
}

You'd use it like this:
Promise.timeout(yourRequestFunctionWhenUserClicksButton(), 1000 * 90); //90 seconds

Basically, if the request lasts more than 90 seconds it will return a rejected promise, otherwise it will fulfill with the value answered from the server.

