You could use an array.

\documentclass{article}
\usepackage{amsmath}
\usepackage{array}
\begin{document}
\[
\begin{array}{c *{10}{@{\;}c}}
S_n &=& (a_1) &+& (a_2)     &+& (a_3)     &+& \cdots &+& (a_1+[n-1]d)\\ 
S_n &=& (a_n) &+& (a_{n-1}) &+& (a_{n-2}) &+& \cdots &+& (a_n+[n-1]d)
